rograms Tuition Campus Life Live. Eat. Play. Athletics Spiritual Life Student Engagement WesQuest Program International Student Resources Parent Resources First Year Experience Veteran Benefits Community The Dunn Center | Official Site Cultural Arts Mims and Gravely Art Galleries Work at Wesleyan Shelton Challenge Rock the Mount Community Event NCWU Summer Camps Event Venue Rentals Administrative and Staff Jobs Community » Careers » Current Openings » Administrative and Staff Jobs Careers at Wesleyan Current Job Openings Administrative & Staff Jobs Graduate Assistant Jobs Faculty Job Openings Full-Time Faculty Positions Adjunct Faculty Positions Applications Download, complete and submit the fillable PDF applications below. Staff Employment Application The University currently has the following job openings: Counselor North Carolina Wesleyan University seeks a motivated individual to serve as Counselor in our Student Affairs program. The Counselor provides basic mental health counseling to students and consultation to University administration regarding student mental health issues. This 10-month position (August to May) also conducts intake and crisis assessments, provides individual counseling sessions, serves on the Behavioral Intervention Team (BIT), and provides educational programs and materials for students as well as faculty and staff. Qualifications include Master’s degree in Counseling, Psychology, or a related field; minimum of three years counseling experience (experience with college students and/or young adults strongly preferred). Anticipated start date: Open until filled To Apply, Download a Staff Application form here > Applications can be submitted email. Please send the following to North Carolina Wesleyan University: A completed application form Cover letter Resume Names and phone numbers of 3 references ATTN: Dr. Jason Modlin Dean of Students jmodlin@ncwu.edu North Carolina Wesleyan University is an equal opportunity employer. North Carolina Wesleyan University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We consider qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, disability, gender identity, protected veteran status, or other protected class. Women, historically underrepresented minorities, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. NC Wesleyan University 3400 N. Wesleyan Blvd. Rocky Mount, NC 27804 252.985.5100 800.488.6292 Contact Us Campus Map All Social Media Channels > Resources My NCWU University Catalog Request More Info Events News Student Email Policies & Notices Title IX and Equal Opportunity Campus Hazing Policy Faculty & Staff Resources Media & Branding Resources Alumni Relations Bishop Beat Newsletter Student Achievement Report Academic Program Inventory Consumer Information Transcript Requests Working at Wesleyan Campus Campus Map & Tour Campus Store Campus Safety Parent Resources The Dunn Center Faculty & Staff Directory Health Services Library Wesleyan News Dining Services Catering Services Event Venue Rentals Dunn Center Rental Space Photo Gallery Apply Request More Info Plan A Visit Give 252.985.5100    |      800.488.6292 ©2026 North Carolina Wesleyan University NCWU About Why NC Wesleyan? Campus Map & Tour Bishop Beliefs We are Battling Bishops Departments Publications Faculty & Staff Directory Contact Us Admissions Apply Visit Tuition Deposit Connect with a Counselor Orientation Financial Aid Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Executive Residency Programs Adult & Online Studies Accelerated Dual Degree Pathways Certificate Programs Partnerships Practical Skills Academy Registrar Library Our Faculty Accreditation & Accountability Adult & Online Adult Undergraduate Programs Adult Studies Tuition Financial Aid Graduate & Professional Programs Graduate Programs Tuition Campus Life Live. Eat. Play. Athletics Spiritual Life Student Engagement WesQuest Program International Student Resources Parent Resources First Ye